  ('loosening-old-grudges', 1, 'Write the old grudge in three sentences, then underline the one part that still stings most.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 2, 'Name the grudge you carry most often in five words or fewer, and write it on a scrap of paper.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 3, 'Notice where in your body the old anger shows up when you think of it: jaw, chest, stomach or hands.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 4, 'Count, roughly, how many times the old story crossed your mind this morning, without judging the number.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 5, 'List three grudges you are carrying, big or small, and circle the one that weighs the most today.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 6, 'Ask yourself how long you have carried this particular resentment, and write down the year it began.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 7, 'Picture the grudge as an object you carry in a bag. What does it look like, and how heavy is it?'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 8, 'Place a hand on the spot where the resentment sits in your body and breathe slowly into it five times.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 9, 'Jot down what the grudge has cost you lately: an hour of sleep, a sour mood, a conversation you avoided.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 10, 'Remind yourself out loud: "Setting this down is for me, and it does not mean what happened was okay."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 11, 'Choose one small grudge, like a rude comment from a stranger, to practice loosening before the bigger ones.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 12, 'Notice what usually sets off the replay: a song, a place, a name, a smell, a date on the calendar.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 13, 'Describe the old anger in one temperature word and one texture word, like hot and sharp or cold and dull.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 14, 'Consider who else knows about this grudge, and whether telling the story to them helps or reopens it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 15, 'Unclench your jaw and drop your shoulders the next time the old memory arrives, then return to what you were doing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 16, 'Make a small pencil mark on a scrap of paper each time the replay shows up this afternoon, just to see its habits.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 17, 'Glance at the clock when the replay starts and again when it ends, just to see how much time it borrows.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 18, 'Wonder what the grudge might be protecting you from, and write the first answer that comes.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 19, 'Finish this sentence in your notebook: "If I stopped carrying this, I worry that..."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 20, 'Check whether the grudge shows up more when you are tired, hungry or lonely, and jot down which.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 21, 'Separate the facts from the feelings: write what a camera would have recorded, then what you felt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 22, 'Say the person''s name quietly to yourself and notice what your breathing does, then take three slow breaths.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 23, 'Write a list of the places, songs or foods you avoid because of this old hurt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 24, 'Before bed, write the grudge on a sticky note, fold it in half, and leave it outside your bedroom door for the night.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 25, 'Recall an hour today when the grudge did not cross your mind at all, and note what you were doing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 26, 'Name one thing you want back that the grudge has taken: easy evenings, a favorite cafe, your sense of humor.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 27, 'Shrug your shoulders up to your ears, hold for five seconds, and let them fall as you breathe out the old story.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 28, 'Figure out how old you were when this happened and how old you are now, and notice the distance between them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 29, 'Give the grudge a plain nickname, like "the parking lot thing," so it takes up less space when it comes up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 30, 'Sort out whether you are angry at what happened, at how it was handled afterward, or both.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 31, 'Catch yourself rehearsing what you would say to them, and stop the rehearsal after the first sentence.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 32, 'Walk around the block once while thinking about the old hurt, and let your pace slow on the way back.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 33, 'Remember one grudge you have already let go of in the past, and write down what helped that happen.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 34, 'Spend two minutes noticing your feet on the floor when the old anger rises at your desk.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 35, 'Make a cup of tea and, while it steeps, name the feeling under the anger: hurt, embarrassment, fear or loss.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 36, 'Put into one sentence what you wish had happened instead, and let yourself feel the wish.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 37, 'Consider whether this grudge connects to an older one, and draw a line between the two on paper.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 38, 'Pay attention to how your mood shifts after you scroll past this person''s name or photo, and decide whether to mute it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 39, 'Tell yourself kindly that it makes sense you are still upset, given how much it mattered.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 40, 'List the ways you have already been carrying this well: you kept working, kept caring, kept going.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 41, 'Stretch your arms overhead in the morning and imagine setting the grudge on a high shelf for the day.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 42, 'Look for the first time this grudge felt lighter, even slightly, and write down when that was.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 43, 'Check in with yourself at lunch: has the old story visited today, and if so, how long did it stay?'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 44, 'Compare how you tell the story to different people, and decide which version feels most true.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 45, 'Copy out the exact words that still echo, then write them again in much smaller handwriting.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 46, 'Sit by a window for three minutes and let the old memory pass through like weather outside the glass.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 47, 'Find one physical habit that comes with the grudge, like a clenched fist or a sigh, and soften it once.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 48, 'Ask yourself whether you are waiting for something from them, an apology or an admission, and name it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 49, 'Write: "I may never get that apology, and I can still have a calmer life." Read it twice.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 50, 'Identify one way the old resentment shows up in your current relationships, like quick suspicion or holding back.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 51, 'Turn off the radio on your drive home and see whether the grudge fills the quiet, then play music you love.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 52, 'Draw a simple timeline from the event to now, marking the stretches when the anger was loudest.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 53, 'Admit what you gain from holding on, like feeling protected or feeling right, and write it down honestly.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 54, 'Breathe in for four counts and out for six when the memory flashes up in a meeting or class.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 55, 'Spot the hour of the day when the replay is strongest, and plan something absorbing for that hour.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 56, 'Pick a grudge that is not about anyone close to you, like a rude store clerk, and decide it can go first.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 57, 'Write a few lines on how the grudge affects your sleep: falling asleep, waking at night, or dreams.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 58, 'Ask yourself, "Is this anger still giving me useful information, or is it just repeating itself?"'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 59, 'Turn what you will no longer put up with into a short list, and keep it as a boundary rather than a weight.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 60, 'Hold a warm mug in both hands when the old hurt comes up, and let the warmth remind you that you are here now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 61, 'Find one thing in the room that did not exist when the old event happened, and let it anchor you in the present.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 62, 'Say "That was then" quietly when the memory pulls you back, and name one thing you see right now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 63, 'Imagine one sign that would tell you the grudge has loosened, like driving past that street without tensing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 64, 'Pause at a red light or a bus stop and check your shoulders for the old tension.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 65, 'Picture the grudge held in a closed fist, then slowly open your actual hand and rest it palm up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 66, 'Think about whether you feel the anger more at home or away from it, and write one guess why.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 67, 'Decide how much of your week the old story deserves, and give it a smaller slot than it takes now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 68, 'Remember that loosening a grudge has no deadline, and write "at my own pace" at the top of today''s page.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 69, 'Retell the old story as if reporting it for a local newspaper, sticking to who, what, where and when.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 70, 'Notice your first thought on waking, and if it is the grudge, get up and open a curtain.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 71, 'Name the two people who have heard about this grudge the most, and consider giving them a break from it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 72, 'Close the evening by writing one line about how the grudge showed up today, then shut the notebook.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 73, 'Say to yourself, "Loosening this does not mean I have to see them or trust them again."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 74, 'Write the event in one column and the story you tell about it in another, like "they didn''t call" beside "they never cared."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 75, 'Underline every "always" and "never" in your account of the old hurt, and try a more exact word for each.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 76, 'Imagine watching the old scene from a balcony far above, and notice what looks different from there.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 77, 'Describe the situation from the point of view of a neutral bystander who saw it happen.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 78, 'Picture yourself ten years from now looking back at this grudge, and write what that older you might say.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 79, 'Consider what else was going on in the other person''s life at the time, without excusing anything they did.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 80, 'Draft a letter to the person that you will never send, saying everything you never got to say.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 81, 'Read an unsent letter out loud once in an empty room, then tear it into small pieces.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 82, 'Compose a second kind of unsent letter, only about how the event affected you, with no questions for them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 83, 'Find a smooth stone, hold it while you name the grudge, and set it down somewhere outdoors to stay.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 84, 'Drop a small stone into a river, lake or stream and watch the ripples settle.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 85, 'Feed a slip of paper with the grudge written on it through a shredder, or tear it by hand into confetti.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 86, 'Burn a note about the old hurt in a safe fire pit or fireplace, with care, and watch the smoke rise.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 87, 'Write the grudge in washable marker on your palm and wash it off slowly with warm water.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 88, 'Mark a fallen leaf with a word for the grudge and let the wind or a stream carry it away.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 89, 'Bury a folded note about the old hurt in a garden bed or flowerpot, and plant a seed on top.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 90, 'Chalk the grudge onto a sidewalk or driveway and let the rain wash it away.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 91, 'Fold an unsent letter into a paper boat, float it in a sink or tub, and let it soak until it comes apart.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 92, 'Pick out one assumption in your story about why they did it, and write two other possible reasons.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 93, 'Sort which parts of the story you know for certain and which parts you have filled in since.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 94, 'Pretend you are telling the old story to a kind stranger on a train, and notice which details you skip.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 95, 'Shrink the old story to a single sentence of twelve words or fewer, and keep that version on a card.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 96, 'Imagine the situation as a scene in a movie, and picture the camera slowly pulling back until the scene is small.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 97, 'Guess what your best friend would say if they heard the story for the first time today, and write it down.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 98, 'If it feels okay, look at a photo from around that time and notice what else was happening in your life then.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 99, 'Write what you might have done in the other person''s shoes on their worst day, without letting them off the hook.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 100, 'Sketch a small map of your whole life and mark the grudge as one spot among many.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 101, 'List five things that happened in the same year as the old hurt that had nothing to do with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 102, 'Wonder whether the person even remembers the event, and notice how that thought lands.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 103, 'Copy this onto a card: "What happened was not okay, and I am allowed to stop replaying it." Read it before breakfast.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 104, 'Tease apart which part of the story is about them and which is about what you came to believe about yourself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 105, 'Write a letter to the younger you who went through it, telling them what you know now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 106, 'List, in an unsent note, only what you no longer want to carry, then fold it and drop it in the recycling.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 107, 'Light a candle, say the grudge out loud once, and blow the candle out when you are ready.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 108, 'Tie a loose knot in a piece of string while naming the old hurt, then untie it slowly.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 109, 'Hold an ice cube while you think of the grudge and watch it melt in your palm over the sink.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 110, 'Trace a word for the old story on the steamy bathroom mirror after a shower and watch it fade.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 111, 'Blow the seeds off a dandelion, or breathe out into cold air, and picture a piece of the grudge going with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 112, 'Clear one object out of a drawer that only reminds you of the old hurt: donate it, recycle it or store it out of sight.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 113, 'Change one thing in your surroundings tied to the memory, like moving a chair or swapping a mug.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 114, 'Imagine the grudge as a radio station and practice turning the volume down a notch in your mind.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 115, 'Begin the story again, this time starting with something you did well during that hard time.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 116, 'Listen for the tense you use: if you tell it in the present tense, retell it once in the past tense.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 117, 'Set down on paper the ending you have been waiting for, then the ending that actually happened, and notice you survived it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 118, 'For a minor grudge, picture the other person as a nervous child on the first day of school, and notice whether anything softens.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 119, 'Imagine unzipping the grudge like a backpack and taking out one stone you no longer need.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 120, 'Draw the grudge as a shape in one color, then draw a much bigger circle around it that stands for the rest of your life.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 121, 'Make a short list of what you know now that you did not know when it happened.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 122, 'Question whether the person''s choice was really about you, or about something going on inside them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 123, 'Hum a song you love while washing dishes, letting the old story take a back seat until the last plate.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 124, 'Look up at the night sky for a minute and notice how small the old event feels against it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 125, 'Stand at the edge of a body of water, or a wide field, and let your eyes rest on the farthest point.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 126, 'Name the moral you have taken from the story, and ask whether it is helping you or narrowing your life.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 127, 'Read your account and swap "they ruined" for "they affected," then notice the difference.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 128, 'Rewrite the grudge as a front-page headline, then rewrite it as a small footnote.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 129, 'Write a four-line poem about the old hurt, and let it be clumsy.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 130, 'Tell the story once to your pet, a plant or an empty chair, then go do something kind for yourself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 131, 'Delete one old message thread you reread to stoke the anger, after saving anything you might need for your records.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 132, 'List three questions you have wanted answered, then write "I can live without the answers" beneath them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 133, 'Hang up your coat tonight and imagine hanging up the heavy coat of the grudge beside it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 134, 'Remember that the old event happened once, while the replay has happened many times, and write that down.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 135, 'Imagine a wise, kind elder listening to your story, and write the one thing they would ask you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 136, 'Think of the event as a chapter, and give the next chapter of your life a title that has nothing to do with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 137, 'Wonder for a minute what the other person might wish they had done differently, without needing them to say it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 138, 'Make two short lists, what the event was and what it was not: it was unfair, and it is not the whole story of you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 139, 'Rinse your hands under running water for a slow count of twenty and imagine the grudge washing off with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 140, 'Pour a glass of water, name the grudge, and give the water to a houseplant so it helps something grow.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 141, 'Crumple a paper with the grudge written on it and toss it into the recycling bin from across the room.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 142, 'Take a walk in a place you have never connected with the old hurt, and let it be a grudge-free zone.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 143, 'Try telling the story with half the anger and twice the kindness toward yourself, and see how it sounds.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 144, 'Imagine the old scene shrinking to the size of a postage stamp, then set it in a corner of your mind.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 145, 'Identify one thing the grudge made you better at, such as spotting unfairness, and keep that skill.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 146, 'End the evening by imagining you are closing a book on the old story, gently, without needing to finish it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 147, 'Choose a short cue phrase, like "Not now, old story," to say when the replay starts.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 148, 'Use a cue phrase the first time the grudge pops up today, and then name one thing you can hear.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 149, 'Set a five-minute timer to think about the grudge on purpose, and when it rings, stand up and move.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 150, 'Schedule ten minutes in the early evening for the old hurt, and when it shows up earlier, tell it to wait.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 151, 'Tap your knee twice as a private signal to step out of the replay, and use it whenever the story starts.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 152, 'Shorten the replay by skipping to the end: "And then it was over, and I am here now."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 153, 'Call or meet a trusted friend and talk the grudge through once, then deliberately change the subject to something fun.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 154, 'Request ten minutes of listening without advice from a friend while you describe the old hurt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 155, 'Let a friend know you would like to stop retelling a certain story, and ask them to gently remind you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 156, 'Note what you learned from what happened, even if the lesson came at too high a price.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 157, 'Start a page with "What I need now is..." and finish the sentence five different ways.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 158, 'Pick one thing you needed back then and did not get, and give a small version of it to yourself today.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 159, 'Decide on one boundary that protects you from a repeat, and write it down instead of carrying the resentment.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 160, 'Repeat to yourself that you can keep your distance from someone and still loosen the grudge inside you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 161, 'If the old hurt involved abuse or still feels overwhelming, write down the name of one trusted person or a licensed counselor you could talk with.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 162, 'Spell out what you would say no to in the future so the old situation cannot repeat itself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 163, 'Catch one moment today when the grudge didn''t bother you, and write down what you were doing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 164, 'Circle the need your anger points at: respect, safety, fairness or care, and write why it fits.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 165, 'Rehearse your cue phrase out loud in the car or the shower, so it is ready when you need it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 166, 'Write the grudge on one side of an index card and your boundary on the other, and keep the boundary side facing up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 167, 'Mute, unfollow or hide one account that keeps reopening the old hurt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 168, 'Prepare what you will say if someone brings up the old event at a gathering, like "I''d rather not get into that."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 169, 'Decide that you no longer have to defend your side of the story to anyone, and notice how that feels.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 170, 'Write what fairness would have looked like then, and what fairness you can give yourself now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 171, 'List three ways you protect yourself now that you couldn''t back then.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 172, 'Remind yourself that forgiveness is optional and personal, and write what, if anything, it means to you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 173, 'Resist the urge to check on the person online by doing something with your hands for five minutes instead.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 174, 'Name one value the event trampled, like honesty or loyalty, and one way you live that value today.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 175, 'Ask yourself, "What would I tell a friend carrying this exact grudge?" and write your answer to yourself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 176, 'Steer a conversation that drifts toward the old hurt to a lighter topic, and notice that you can.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 177, 'Whisper "I''m choosing my peace" when you catch yourself rehearsing an old argument.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 178, 'Make a short playlist of three songs that help you feel steady, and play it when the old story gets loud.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 179, 'Write a list of what you will not let this event decide for you anymore, like where you shop or what you wear.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 180, 'Take back one small thing the grudge took, like visiting a park you avoided, if it is safe to do so.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 181, 'Plan how you would like to respond, not react, if you ever cross paths with the person by chance.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 182, 'Explore whether part of you believes holding the grudge keeps it from happening again, and write a boundary that does that job better.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 183, 'Think about what you need to feel safe now, and take one small practical step toward it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 184, 'Picture the replay as a train passing a station: you notice it go by, and you stay on the platform.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 185, 'Stop the replay at the first scene today and say, "I know how this one ends."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 186, 'Reach out to a counselor, faith leader or support group if this grudge sits on top of something painful you have never had help with.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 187, 'Record in a few lines what you are proud of in how you handled what came after.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 188, 'Spend fifteen minutes on a hobby that absorbs you fully, and let the grudge wait outside.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 189, 'Write a release list of small habits from the old event you are ready to drop, like checking for their car.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 190, 'Ask a trusted person, "Have I been telling this story a lot?" and take the answer kindly.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 191, 'Reflect on whether you seek out people who agree the other person was wrong, and what you hope to get from them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 192, 'Write one sentence about what you would like your life to be full of instead of this grudge.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 193, 'Change the subject in your own head: when the replay starts, plan tonight''s dinner in detail.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 194, 'Swap "I can''t believe they did that" for "That happened, and I''m handling it" when the thought comes up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 195, 'Thank yourself out loud for every time today you set the replay down, even for a minute.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 196, 'Honor the younger you who was hurt in a way other than holding the grudge, like a kind note or a favorite meal.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 197, 'Keep a sentence in your phone notes for if the person contacts you and you don''t want to engage.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 198, 'Take a slow sip of water each time the old argument starts in your head, as a cue to come back.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 199, 'Look for one way to make the old situation less likely to happen to someone else, like a kinder workplace habit.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 200, 'Write a list of who in your life you trust now, and how they earned it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 201, 'Give yourself permission to feel angry for five full minutes, then wash your face and move on to the next thing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 202, 'Compare a current situation that feels like the old one, and write down two ways it is actually different.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 203, 'Turn what the grudge has taught you about your limits into one clear sentence.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 204, 'Ask yourself whether letting go feels like losing, and write what you would actually lose.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 205, 'Pause before telling the old story to someone new today, and decide whether it needs telling.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 206, 'Prepare a phrase for a relative who keeps bringing up the old hurt, like "I''m working on setting that down."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 207, 'Picture a door closing softly on the old scene as you leave work, and walk through your real front door fresh.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 208, 'Lean on the friends who leave you feeling lighter after you talk, more than the ones who stir it up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 209, 'Scan your calendar for the coming days and plan something pleasant on a date that is usually hard.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 210, 'Divide a page into what you can control now and what you could never control back then, three items each.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 211, 'Make a rule for yourself: you can talk about the grudge, but only while walking, and the walk ends the talk.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 212, 'Carry a cue phrase on a small card in your wallet and touch it when the old anger stirs.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 213, 'Draft a boundary like "I don''t discuss that person at work," adjust it to fit you, and use it once.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 214, 'Choose what you''d rather spend the replay time on, and put that activity on your list for tonight.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 215, 'Let yourself say "I''m not ready" if part of you resists loosening this grudge, and write what would help.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 216, 'Leave a one-line note for your future self: "You don''t owe anyone a quick recovery."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 217, 'Describe out loud three colors you can see right now when the old story starts.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 218, 'Spend one minute imagining your life with the grudge one size smaller, and notice what space opens.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 219, 'Trace how the old hurt changed what you look for in friends or partners, and keep the parts that protect you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 220, 'Write down a small grudge you carry, like the friend who forgot your birthday, and decide whether it still deserves space.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 221, 'Think of a coworker who once took credit for your work, and write what you want to remember about your own contribution.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 222, 'Recall an old comment from a sibling that still pinches, and write it down so it isn''t only living in your head.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 223, 'Bring to mind a neighbor you''ve been quietly annoyed with for years, and name one ordinary thing they do well.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 224, 'Remember a driver who cut you off long ago while you sat in the passenger seat, and smile at how long it stuck around.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 225, 'Picture a rude stranger from years back and wish them, silently, a better day than the one you met them on.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 226, 'Name a grudge you hold against yourself, and write it the way you would describe a friend''s mistake.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 227, 'Address a short note of understanding to the younger you who made that choice with what they knew at the time.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 228, 'List three people who have treated you well over the years, and let yourself feel grateful for one of them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 229, 'Send a thank-you text to someone who has been reliably kind to you, with no mention of the old hurt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 230, 'Accept that you still feel angry sometimes, and tell yourself feelings don''t run on a schedule.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 231, 'Think of a former boss you still resent, and write one skill you built in spite of them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 232, 'Write about an ex you still feel stung by: one thing you learned about what you want, and one thing you will never accept again.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 233, 'Recall a teacher or coach who embarrassed you once, and tell the younger you, "That was about them, not your worth."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 234, 'Think of a friend who drifted away without explanation, and write what the friendship gave you while it lasted.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 235, 'Pick a petty grudge, like the person who never returned your book, and declare it officially retired.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 236, 'Remember a restaurant or store that treated you badly, and decide whether you want to keep avoiding it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 237, 'Name one mistake you keep punishing yourself for, and write down what you did afterward to make things better.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 238, 'Place a hand on your heart and say, "I did the best I could with what I knew then."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 239, 'Put the grudge against yourself on paper, then write beside it what you would need to hear from a kind friend.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 240, 'Notice someone today who holds a door, lets you merge or smiles, and let that small kindness count.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 241, 'Jot one line about each person who showed up for you during a hard time, and read the list slowly.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 242, 'Thank a current coworker for one specific thing, and notice the good people in your working life.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 243, 'Hold back the impulse to bring up an old slight with a friend or partner, and ask whether it still matters today.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 244, 'Recall an old fight with a roommate, and write one thing you''d do differently now and one thing they should have.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 245, 'Think of a relative who said something hurtful at a past gathering, and plan one way to protect your peace at the next one.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 246, 'Forgive yourself for one small thing today, like a forgotten call or a sharp reply, and say so out loud.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 247, 'Remember a time you were the one who hurt someone, and notice that you have grown since then.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 248, 'Tell yourself, "I can be angry and kind to myself at the same time."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 249, 'Offer yourself a small comfort when the old anger visits: a blanket, a warm shower or a favorite snack.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 250, 'Recall a group project that left you doing all the work, and write how you''d protect your time now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 251, 'Think of a friend who once broke a confidence, and decide what you will share with them, if anything, from here on.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 252, 'Remember someone who gave you the benefit of the doubt, and consider giving a small grudge the same.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 253, 'Write a few words about a person who made you feel seen this year, and stick them on your fridge.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 254, 'Revisit a story you tell about your own past failures, and soften one harsh adjective in it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 255, 'Take yourself for a walk as you would a friend who was hurting, at an easy pace, with no fixing.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 256, 'Think of an online stranger whose comment still bugs you, and notice how little you actually know about them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 257, 'Ask yourself whether you are holding yourself to a standard you would never hold anyone else to.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 258, 'If it feels true, write down one thing a parent or caregiver did right, even if there is plenty they got wrong.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 259, 'Let go of one tiny grudge today, like the person who took your parking spot, by wishing them a smooth trip.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 260, 'Name a landlord, service provider or company you still fume about, and decide whether a complaint letter or a deep breath is the better use of your energy.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 261, 'Recall a friend who forgot something important to you, and write about two times they did show up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 262, 'Speak kindly to yourself in the mirror about the grudge you hold against yourself: "You are allowed to grow."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 263, 'Keep a short list of the people whose kindness outweighs the hurt you carry, and read it before sleep.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 264, 'Catch yourself treating a new person with caution because of someone in the past, and give them a small fresh chance.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 265, 'Think back to a time someone let a grudge against you go, and how it felt to be on that side.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 266, 'Picture a classmate who left you out long ago, and write one thing you''d tell your school-age self about friendship.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 267, 'Name an old grudge against your hometown or a former school, and recall one good memory from that place.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 268, 'Allow yourself a rest from working on the grudge today, and do something purely enjoyable.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 269, 'Thank a friend who listened to the old story many times, and tell them how much it helped.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 270, 'Recall a grudge you once held that turned out to rest on a misunderstanding, and what cleared it up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 271, 'Write yourself the apology you wish you had received, and sign it with care.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 272, 'Do one generous thing for someone unrelated to the old hurt, and notice that kindness still flows through you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 273, 'Remember an old game or contest you think was judged unfairly, and grin at how long that call has lived in your head.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 274, 'Imagine making the same mistake today that you made back then, and write what you would say to yourself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 275, 'Settle one grudge about money owed by choosing to ask once more, write it off, or set a limit for next time.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 276, 'Remember a party or celebration you weren''t invited to, and write how you''d like to feel about it now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 277, 'Give yourself credit for being someone who cares deeply, which is part of why this still hurts.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 278, 'Think of a person who apologized to you well in the past, and notice how good that repair felt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 279, 'Hold a photo of yourself from back then, if you have one, and say something gentle to that person.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 280, 'Choose a grudge against yourself about your body, health or habits, and write one forgiving fact beside it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 281, 'List a few times you have been forgiven for small things, and notice how ordinary forgiveness can be.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 282, 'Let a small annoyance today, like a slow line, pass without adding it to your old collection.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 283, 'Write the name of someone who treated you with respect at your hardest job, and recall one thing they did.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 284, 'Check whether you are kinder to strangers than to yourself about the old event, and even it out a little.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 285, 'Send a kind message to someone who was also hurt by the same event, if you are in touch and it feels right.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 286, 'Question one grudge you inherited from someone else''s story, like an old family feud, and ask whether it is yours to carry.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 287, 'Set aside a warm drink, a soft chair and ten quiet minutes tonight for the part of you that is still hurting.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 288, 'Remember a time you were short with a stranger on a bad day, and extend that understanding to someone who was short with you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 289, 'Write down five qualities you like in yourself that the old hurt never touched.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 290, 'Think of a mentor or teacher who believed in you, and write them a thank-you you may or may not send.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 291, 'Ask yourself whether there is anyone you want a fresh start with, and remember that the answer can be no.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 292, 'Spot one moment today when you felt free of every grudge, big or small, and note where you were.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 293, 'Before a family gathering or holiday, decide on one topic you will gently steer away from if the old hurt comes up.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 294, 'Plan a quiet escape at the next family event, like a short walk or helping in the kitchen, for when old feelings stir.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 295, 'Mark the anniversary of the old event on your calendar with something kind for yourself instead of the memory.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 296, 'As a new year approaches, write down one old grudge you would like to carry less into the months ahead.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 297, 'When a holiday stirs up an old family hurt, give yourself permission to celebrate in a smaller, quieter way.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 298, 'Sketch a gentle plan for the date that still stings each year: who you''ll be with, where you''ll go, what you''ll eat.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 299, 'Look back over this challenge so far and write down one small change in how the old story visits.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 300, 'Consider whether a fresh start with someone is something you want, and only if it feels safe, write what a first small step might be.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 301, 'Remember that reconnecting is never required, and write "I can wish them well from a distance" to see if it fits.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 302, 'Watch how the light or weather is changing this season, and let it remind you that old feelings can change too.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 303, 'Sit outside at dawn or dusk for five minutes and let the old grudge stay at the edge of your attention.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 304, 'On a long drive, choose an audiobook or podcast that absorbs you instead of letting the old argument fill the miles.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 305, 'While waiting in line, notice if the old story starts, and read the labels on what''s around you instead.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 306, 'In the shower, let the water run over your shoulders and picture the old tension rinsing down the drain.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 307, 'On a walk, breathe out slowly every fourth step and let the old story fall a little further behind each time.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 308, 'On a rainy afternoon, leave a note about the grudge on the windowsill while you make something warm to drink.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 309, 'During your commute, pick a landmark that, once you pass it, means the old story is set down until you get home.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 310, 'At bedtime, list three ordinary good things from today so the old hurt isn''t the last thing on your mind.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 311, 'When the season of the old event comes around, watch for early signs like poor sleep or a short fuse, and go easier on yourself.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 312, 'If an old hurt ever leaves you feeling unsafe or in crisis, call or text 988 any time of day to talk with someone right away.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 313, 'At a family meal, choose a seat that feels comfortable for you, and let that be enough.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 314, 'When old photos come out at a gathering, step away for a minute if you need to, and return when you are ready.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 315, 'Write a list of the traditions that still feel good to you, and keep those even if others are tangled with the old hurt.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 316, 'Start a new tradition for a hard date, like a hike, a movie or cooking a favorite meal.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 317, 'On the first day of a new season, write one sentence about who you are becoming apart from the old story.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 318, 'Name one place or person that feels a little less charged than it did when you started this challenge.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 319, 'Reread any early notes you kept about this grudge, and notice what has softened and what hasn''t.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 320, 'Write a letter of appreciation to yourself for the effort you''ve put into setting this down.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 321, 'Accept whether the old grudge has gotten quieter, louder or stayed the same lately, without arguing with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 322, 'Plant a bulb or seed and let its slow growth stand for the slow work of letting go.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 323, 'For a reunion or wedding where the person might be, plan a short exit line and a friend to stay near, and keep your distance if you want it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 324, 'Wear something you love to an event where old feelings may surface, as a small reminder of who you are now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 325, 'On a birthday, yours or theirs, notice the old feeling and give yourself a gift of unhurried time.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 326, 'Practice a short, calm answer for when someone asks why you don''t talk to a certain person: "We''re not in touch, and I''m okay with that."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 327, 'If you want a fresh start with someone who never harmed you, write the first sentence you''d say, then wait a few days before deciding whether to say it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 328, 'Imagine running into the person at a store by chance, and rehearse a calm nod as you walk on.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 329, 'Search your memory for a grudge you have already outgrown and simply forgot to put down, and put it down now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 330, 'Watch a sunrise or sunset from start to finish and let it be a small ceremony for something you''re ready to release.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 331, 'Sit with your morning coffee or tea and choose one word for how you want to feel about the old hurt by evening.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 332, 'On a quiet evening, play a song that once reminded you of the old event, only if it feels okay, and let it become just a song again.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 333, 'On a weekend morning, cook a breakfast you love and let it be time the grudge doesn''t get.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 334, 'Take a short trip to a new place, even a nearby town, and notice that the old story feels farther away.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 335, 'When a scent pulls up the old memory, breathe in something pleasant right after, like coffee or citrus.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 336, 'At work, if the old grudge involves a colleague, keep your focus on your own tasks and guard your energy.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 337, 'On a sleepless night, get up, write the replaying thoughts on paper, and go back to bed a little lighter.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 338, 'Imagine what you would do with all the energy the grudge used to take, and spend ten minutes doing it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 339, 'Put any keepsakes still tied to the old hurt into one box, label it, and store it somewhere you rarely go.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 340, 'Write down what letting go does not mean for you: it does not mean excusing them, trusting them or calling them.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 341, 'Put into three short lines what letting go does mean for you, in your own words.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 342, 'Picture letting go as something that happens in layers, and name the layer you are working on now.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 343, 'Plan something to look forward to in the coming month that has nothing to do with the past.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 344, 'Visit a library, museum or garden and let your attention rest on things much older than any grudge.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 345, 'Give the old story a ten-second shrug when it appears at the end of a long day, and go to bed.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 346, 'On a cold morning, warm your hands and say one thing you''re ready to stop holding.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 347, 'In the heat of summer, cool your face with water and imagine the old anger cooling along with it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 348, 'When autumn leaves fall, notice that trees let go without forcing it, and let that be your pace.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 349, 'Before a phone call with a relative you find hard, set a time limit and plan something pleasant for afterward.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 350, 'When the person''s name comes up in conversation, breathe once, and let the talk move on without you adding to it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 351, 'Create a small closing ritual for this stretch of work on the grudge: a walk, a meal, a candle, whatever fits you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 352, 'Write down three ways your life is bigger now than it was when the hurt happened.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 353, 'Decide whether you want to keep loosening this grudge or rest from it for a while, knowing both are okay.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 354, 'Turn gently to a different grudge if this one has eased, or stay with this one if it hasn''t.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 355, 'Write a short good wish for your own future, free of the old story.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 356, 'Tell a trusted friend one way you feel lighter, and let them celebrate it with you.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 357, 'Pick a song that feels like moving forward and play it while you tidy one corner of your home.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 358, 'Look at your hands and remember all the things they''ve built, held and cared for since the old event.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 359, 'Imagine the person who hurt you living their own life far away from yours, and let the distance feel like relief.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 360, 'Remember that peace doesn''t require the other person to change, and do one thing you enjoy regardless.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 361, 'At the start of a new week, set an intention: "I''ll notice the old story and let it pass."'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 362, 'Keep a note of the smallest sign that the grudge has loosened, like a laugh where you used to tense, somewhere you''ll see it.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 363, 'Tell yourself, "Whatever is left of this, I''ll carry more lightly," and go about your day.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 364, 'Describe in one sentence the kind of person you are when you aren''t carrying old anger.'),
  ('loosening-old-grudges', 365, 'Close your notebook on the old story tonight with a simple line: "This is mine to set down, a little at a time."')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
